sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0257 (task group modes), docs/reference/tasks.md#task-group-modes. A scheduled Gateway command like task:pr-gate: it reads the Gateway's own records and admits the existing tasks.publish (docs/cli/task/publish.mmd) behind every guard of a manual publish. It starts no other work and merges nothing. The tick is a scheduled command, not an Operation kind: like instance/container/thread.mmd it names `kind: none`, and the Operation it admits is `tasks.publish`.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · task:pr-when-done schedule
  %% kind: none
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane GH icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Task copy<br/>on its Node
  participant GH as GitHub<br/>repository · PRs
  Note over GW: Tick every minute<br/>task:pr-when-done
  %%> When:
  %%> - every minute while the Tasks extension is on, as one scheduled Gateway command beside `task:pr-gate`
  %%> Why:
  %%> - a group becomes done when the caller completes its last subtask, which ends no Operation; one tick reads the whole rule in one place and survives a lost callback or a worker restart
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no command: no person starts the tick; a person releases a waiting group with `task:publish GROUP`
  Note over GW: Find the done groups<br/>own records only
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - takes each open group whose workspace is a task copy and that has no pull request
  %%> - keeps a group whose work is done: every subtask ended and one completed; the last completed one has an eligible passed handoff check, and no newer handoff check exists; the reviewer thread's newest turn reviewed exactly that commit and ended `done` (a subtask of a task copy cannot be completed while a turn runs); no turn may still run and no Operation of the group runs
  %%> - keeps a group whose mode now resolves to `pr_when_done` (group, then Project, then Gateway) and whose done check recorded `pr_when_done` when it passed
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a group in `review_before_pr`, or whose done check recorded it, stays `waiting_for_release`; nothing happens on GitHub
  %%> - a done group whose reviewer thread's newest turn sent no pull request text stays `waiting_for_pr_text`; the tick admits nothing and stores nothing
  Note over GW: Admit the publish<br/>pr-when-done:GROUP:CHECK
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts the `tasks.publish` admission of `task:publish` with the done check, the reviewer's title and body that its newest turn recorded on the done check (with `Closes #N` for a group that names issue N), and a ready pull request
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - every guard of a manual publish: the group lock, the copy publish allow list, the eligible candidate, the running container
  %%> - the key `pr-when-done:GROUP:CHECK` was not admitted before, and no publish of this check failed or was cancelled; a repeat tick starts nothing
  %%> - after a lock timeout, the key adds its attempt, `pr-when-done:GROUP:CHECK:2` or `:3`, while fewer than 3 publishes of this check timed out on a lock
  %%> - inside the admission's transaction, after the group's row lock, the group is still done with this check and still in `pr_when_done`, else `tasks.not_done`
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #TASK recorded, kind `tasks.publish`, caller `gateway:pr-when-done`
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-publish
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts the publish run that `docs/cli/task/publish.mmd` shows, unchanged
  SW->>N: Export the copy<br/>workspace phase · bundle
  %%> How:
  %%> - the copy's checkout HEAD must be the done check's commit; the bundle comes to the worker and the copy never holds a token
  %%> - the workspace phase is the behavior `task-workspace-NODE-GROUP`, and every publish step names its group too, so the publish of another group on this Node never waits for its lock
  Note over SW: Check the .env content
  %%> How:
  %%> - the `.env` path and content checks, with the Club key of a nested-fleet copy, run before any token exists; the reviewer's title and body are checked too
  SW->>GH: Push and open the PR<br/>task-GROUP · ready
  %%> How:
  %%> - the push step mints its own token; the pull request opens ready, not as a draft
  alt published
    GH-->>SW: Branch pushed · PR number
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record the publication<br/>pr_url · state published
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the group's `publication` state is `published`; the group keeps its status and its task copy
    %%> - Orbit never merges this pull request (`tasks.copy_pr_no_merge` on every merge path); a person merges it on GitHub
  else lock timed out
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>a step's lock timed out
    %%> When:
    %%> - a step waited 60 s for a behavior lock that another run held: `Lock "…/.lock" held by … — timed out after …ms`
    Note over GW: Retry the done check<br/>attempt 2 or 3 · next tick
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Operation keeps `tasks.publish_lock_timeout`; the group's `publication` stays `publishing`
    %%> - the next tick admits the same done check again under the key with its attempt, behind every guard of the first
    %%> - after the third lock timeout the publication shows `refused` with `tasks.publish_lock_timeout`; `task:publish GROUP` tries again
    %%> Why:
    %%> - nothing on the copy or on GitHub was wrong; a lock timeout says only that a step was busy
  else refused
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> When:
    %%> - a step failed, such as `tasks.publish_secret_content` or `tasks.push_failed`; any failure but a lock timeout
    %%> - an admission refusal, such as `tasks.copy_publish_held` or `tasks.commit_not_checked`, starts no run and ends here too
    %%> - a stopped task copy refuses at admission with `tasks.instance_not_running` and is stored too
    %%> - only `operation.target_busy`, `tasks.copy_turn_unended` and `tasks.not_done` are no refusal: the next tick reads the group again and stores nothing
    %%> - a fault that is no refusal is stored as `tasks.publish_failed`; a refusal is never stored over a publish admitted in between
    Note over GW: Show the refusal<br/>state refused · error_code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - an admission refusal is stored on the group; a failed, interrupted or cancelled publish of the done check, by any caller, keeps its code on its Operation (`operation.cancelled` when it has none); `task:show` and `task:status` show `refused` with the code
    %%> - the group keeps its status, and the task copy and its checked commit stay
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - the tick does not start the same done check again; a new handoff check or `task:publish GROUP` tries again
    %%> - a hand `task:publish GROUP` of the same check is admitted at any time no Operation of the group runs
  end
